<Routine Name="SCL_DINT" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Scale Value
(all DINT)
In1=Source
In2=Rate
In3=Offset
Out1=Destination]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[
All information provided  - No Warranty or implied merchantability. 
Refer to the RSLogix 5000 End User License Agreement (EULA) in the Release Notes

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[SBR(SCL_DINT.Source,SCL_DINT.Rate,SCL_DINT.Offset)NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This routine performs the operation of the SLC-500 Scale With Parameters instruction (SCL).

Use this routine to scale data from your analog module and bring it into the limits prescribed by the process variable or another analog module.  For example, use SCL to convert a 4-20 mA input signal to a PID process variable.  Or use SCL to scale an analog input to control an analog output.

When rung conditions are true, this instruction multiplies the source by a specified rate.  The rounded result is added to an offset value and placed in the destination.

Scaled value = (input value x rate) + offset
Rate = (scaled max. - scaled min.) / (input max. - input min.)
Offset = scaled minimum - (input minimum x rate)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Scaled value = (input value x rate) + offset]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MUL(SCL_DINT.Source,SCL_DINT.Rate,SCL_DINT.Local_Temp1)ADD(SCL_DINT.Local_Temp1,SCL_DINT.Offset,SCL_DINT.Destination);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[RET(SCL_DINT.Destination);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="SCL_REAL" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Scale Value 
(all REAL)
In1=Source
In2=Rate
In3=Offset
Out1=Destination]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[
All information provided  - No Warranty or implied merchantability. 
Refer to the RSLogix 5000 End User License Agreement (EULA) in the Release Notes

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[SBR(SCL_REAL.Source,SCL_REAL.Rate,SCL_REAL.Offset)NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This routine performs the operation of the SLC-500 Scale With Parameters instruction (SCL).

Use this routine to scale data from your analog module and bring it into the limits prescribed by the process variable or another analog module.  For example, use SCL to convert a 4-20 mA input signal to a PID process variable.  Or use SCL to scale an analog input to control an analog output.

When rung conditions are true, this instruction multiplies the source by a specified rate.  The rounded result is added to an offset value and placed in the destination.

Scaled value = (input value x rate) + offset
Rate = (scaled max. - scaled min.) / (input max. - input min.)
Offset = scaled minimum - (input minimum x rate)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Scaled value = (input value x rate) + offset]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MUL(SCL_REAL.Source,SCL_REAL.Rate,SCL_REAL.Destination)ADD(SCL_REAL.Destination,SCL_REAL.Offset,SCL_DINT.Destination);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[RET(SCL_REAL.Destination);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="SCP_DINT" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Scale with Prarams (all Real)
In1=Source
In2=InMin
In3=InMax
In4=ScaleMin
In5=ScaleMax
Out1=Destination]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[
All information provided  - No Warranty or implied merchantability. 
Refer to the RSLogix 5000 End User License Agreement (EULA) in the Release Notes

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[SBR(SCP_DINT.Input,SCP_DINT.InputMin,SCP_DINT.InpuMax,SCP_DINT.ScaledMin,SCP_DINT.ScaledMax)NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This routine performs the operation of the SLC-500 Scale With Parameters instruction (SCP).

This output instruction consists of six parameters.  Parameters may be integer immediate data values or tags containing values.  The Input value is scaled to a range determined by creating a linear relationship between input min and max values and scaled min and max values.  The scaled result is returned to the tag indicated by the output parameter.

The formula is as follows:
Scaled value = (input value x rate) + offset
Rate = (scaled max. - scaled min.) / (input max. - input min.)
Offset = scaled minimum - (input minimum x rate)
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Rate = (scaled max. - scaled min.) / (input max. - input min.)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[SUB(SCP_DINT.ScaledMax,SCP_DINT.ScaledMin,SCP_DINT.Local_Temp1)SUB(SCP_DINT.InpuMax,SCP_DINT.InputMin,SCP_DINT.Local_Temp2)DIV(SCP_DINT.Local_Temp1,SCP_DINT.Local_Temp2,SCP_DINT.Local_Rate);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Offset = scaled minimum - (input minimum x rate)]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MUL(SCP_DINT.InputMin,SCP_DINT.Local_Rate,SCP_DINT.Local_Temp3)SUB(SCP_DINT.ScaledMin,SCP_DINT.Local_Temp3,SCP_DINT.Local_Offset);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Scaled value = (input value x rate) + offset]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[MUL(SCP_DINT.Input,SCP_DINT.Local_Rate,SCP_DINT.Local_Temp4)ADD(SCP_DINT.Local_Temp4,SCP_DINT.Local_Offset,SCP_DINT.Local_Out);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(SCP_DINT.Local_Out,SCP_DINT.Output)RET(SCP_DINT.Output);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="SCP_REAL" Type="RLL">
<Description>
<![CDATA[Scale with Params (all REAL)
In1=Source
In2=InMin
In3=InMax
In4=ScaleMin
In5=ScaleMax
Out1=Destination]]>
</Description>
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[
